<p>Russia launched a large wave of drones and missiles across Ukraine on Sunday, striking targets that Ukrainian officials and media reports said included energy infrastructure, railways, and residential areas. Kyiv was among the hardest hit. President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said Russia fired 297 drones and nearly 50 missiles, and that Ukrainian air defences shot down a “significant proportion” of them. The strikes came just ahead of the fourth anniversary of Russia’s full-scale invasion (February 24, 2022) and shortly after another round of U.S.-mediated talks aimed at ending the war, according to reporting. Reports on casualties varied by location and outlet. Zelenskyy again urged allies to provide more air-defence support, arguing Ukraine needs stronger protection for its cities and critical services.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/KziZbMDuVURYwoDUx7GqncTzY9T7CtKopko7GcZcNJ7QcVes1gx5PCId66ZsWkrs3MRGVkuqgfL5P0S9yPgybV5hkHlJfNWZBW5CO-rceohzQzprJk35VuBdBZt-saFxfqHgYzspXPSuMlrO5NTIRhtVCz97bSdIopJ5WDhlvw7K9HR_kZ3w3hOaelBa1TktRANGRgDHSCSNf_BHpvlTlZk_42M8nD2T39joa2tA44cJQvFhGB6vq0Ayt_oie4MFZiKu81qhVNBI1NI' alt='' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Air defence push: Zelenskyy said “Moscow continues to invest in strikes more than diplomacy” as he urged allies to bolster Ukraine’s air defences.</li><li>Recent pattern: The Hindu said Kyiv has faced waves of overnight missile and drone strikes in recent weeks, and has been a frequent target since the start of the invasion.</li><li>House destroyed: The Guardian said a residential house in Kyiv was flattened in the attacks.</li><li>Frontline evolution: An FT visual report said drones are reshaping the frontline “kill zone,” changing tactics and offering a glimpse of how future wars may be fought.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy: He said “Moscow continues to invest in strikes more than diplomacy” and called for stronger air defences. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/22/russia-missiles-ukraine-hungary-block-eu-sanctions'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>The New York Times: The paper said at least one man was killed in Kyiv as Russia launched a wave of drones and missiles that also struck areas around Lviv. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/22/world/europe/ukraine-russia-attacks-lviv.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Financial Times (battlefield analysis): The report said the spread of drones has created a lethal “kill zone” along the frontline, shrinking reaction times and changing how troops move and resupply. (<a href='https://ig.ft.com/ukraine-kill-zone/'>Financial Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/video/russia-launches-another-large-scale-attack-against-ukraine/'>Russia launches another large-scale attack against Ukraine</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://ig.ft.com/ukraine-kill-zone/'>Inside Ukraine’s ‘kill zone’</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/22/world/europe/ukraine-russia-attacks-lviv.html'>Russia Attacks Ukraine Ahead of Invasion’s 4th Anniversary</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/russian-drone-strike-on-ukraine-zaporizhzhia-war-updates/article70665751.ece'>Russian overnight strikes across Ukraine kill three</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/22/russia-missiles-ukraine-hungary-block-eu-sanctions'>Russia fires scores of missiles at Ukraine as Hungary threatens to block EU sanctions</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>